## Structure

```
src/
├── app.py                                    <- Flask app factory
├── config/settings.py                        <- env loading
├── errors/app_error.py                       <- error classes
├── shared/database/sqlalchemy.py             <- ORM setup
├── domain/<module>/
│   ├── entity.py                             <- domain entity (pure Python)
│   ├── repository.py                         <- repository interface (ABC)
│   └── service.py                            <- domain service
├── application/<module>/
│   ├── use_case.py                           <- use cases
│   └── dto.py                                <- DTOs
└── infrastructure/
    ├── persistence/<module>_repository.py    <- persistence adapter
    └── web/<module>_router.py               <- Flask blueprint
```

Call direction: `infrastructure -> application -> domain`. Domain never imports
from infrastructure or application.

